{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01187",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.79,
      "end_seconds": 4.64,
      "duration_seconds": 3.85,
      "text": "Sorry I'm a little late, you know, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.56,
      "end_seconds": 11.1,
      "duration_seconds": 4.54,
      "text": "Yes, come in and sit down. What brings you here today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 12.24,
      "end_seconds": 21.24,
      "duration_seconds": 9.0,
      "text": "I'm here because of pain going into the buttock. I didn't want to bother you but it keeps coming back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 22.22,
      "end_seconds": 25.36,
      "duration_seconds": 3.14,
      "text": "What's the timeline, when did it begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 26.46,
      "end_seconds": 28.36,
      "duration_seconds": 1.9,
      "text": "Probably two days. Yeah."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 29.74,
      "end_seconds": 33.85,
      "duration_seconds": 4.11,
      "text": "So, would you say mild, moderate or severe?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 35.92,
      "end_seconds": 44.65,
      "duration_seconds": 8.73,
      "text": "Mostly severe. Yeah, I've had pain in my lower back too, for about three months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 45.21,
      "end_seconds": 51.53,
      "duration_seconds": 6.32,
      "text": "Have you had pain going into the buttock before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 52.56,
      "end_seconds": 57.62,
      "duration_seconds": 5.06,
      "text": "A bit, last year. It settled by itself back then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 58.16,
      "end_seconds": 60.9,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "And bladder problems, any of that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 62.31,
      "end_seconds": 66.08,
      "duration_seconds": 3.77,
      "text": "Erm, not at all, no bladder problems."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 66.32,
      "end_seconds": 74.57,
      "duration_seconds": 8.25,
      "text": "Mm, okay. Let me check a few things. Any weight loss, weakness in the legs or numbness in the legs?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 76.6,
      "end_seconds": 79.45,
      "duration_seconds": 2.85,
      "text": "No, nothing to report there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 81.37,
      "end_seconds": 84.05,
      "duration_seconds": 2.68,
      "text": "Is your urine normal, no changes?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 84.7,
      "end_seconds": 86.22,
      "duration_seconds": 1.52,
      "text": "Nothing there, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 104.63,
      "end_seconds": 108.59,
      "duration_seconds": 3.96,
      "text": "Okay, is there anything relevant on the family side?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 109.24,
      "end_seconds": 111.64,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "My uncle has high cholesterol."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 113.55,
      "end_seconds": 115.91,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "Anything you do to stay fit?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 117.57,
      "end_seconds": 121.02,
      "duration_seconds": 3.45,
      "text": "I do a yoga class on Thursdays."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 122.53,
      "end_seconds": 124.51,
      "duration_seconds": 1.98,
      "text": "Tell me about your eating."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 125.23,
      "end_seconds": 131.18,
      "duration_seconds": 5.95,
      "text": "I drink a lot of tea and snack through the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 132.82,
      "end_seconds": 135.35,
      "duration_seconds": 2.53,
      "text": "Right, who lives with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 135.85,
      "end_seconds": 138.55,
      "duration_seconds": 2.7,
      "text": "My partner and our baby."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 150.6,
      "end_seconds": 154.41,
      "duration_seconds": 3.81,
      "text": "Tell me about any past illnesses or ongoing conditions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 155.35,
      "end_seconds": 158.55,
      "duration_seconds": 3.2,
      "text": "I've had high blood pressure, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 160.52,
      "end_seconds": 166.36,
      "duration_seconds": 5.84,
      "text": "Mm, okay. Are you allergic to anything? Any allergies to medicines or foods?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 167.82,
      "end_seconds": 171.71,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "Uh, no, I'm not allergic to anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 173.21,
      "end_seconds": 176.57,
      "duration_seconds": 3.36,
      "text": "Did you ever have any procedures done?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 177.48,
      "end_seconds": 181.47,
      "duration_seconds": 3.99,
      "text": "I had a varicose vein procedure last year."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 182.44,
      "end_seconds": 185.84,
      "duration_seconds": 3.4,
      "text": "What do you take on a normal day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 187.55,
      "end_seconds": 196.95,
      "duration_seconds": 9.4,
      "text": "I take valsartan, 80 milligrams, once a day for my blood pressure. Paracetamol, 500 milligrams, when needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 198.5,
      "end_seconds": 201.29,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "Let's start with the basic checks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 211.97,
      "end_seconds": 214.7,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "That's it, just a little longer..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 224.91,
      "end_seconds": 231.06,
      "duration_seconds": 6.15,
      "text": "Okay: saturation 97 percent, respiratory rate 17, heart rate 80, pressure 120 over 72."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 232.9,
      "end_seconds": 234.41,
      "duration_seconds": 1.51,
      "text": "Is that okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 235.98,
      "end_seconds": 245.95,
      "duration_seconds": 9.97,
      "text": "Right, I'll interpret them after the examination. Going by what you've described, this looks most like mechanical low back pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 246.64,
      "end_seconds": 248.16,
      "duration_seconds": 1.52,
      "text": "Is this permanent?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 249.61,
      "end_seconds": 269.8,
      "duration_seconds": 20.19,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like mechanical low back pain, but I'd like to confirm. So, to recap quickly. You've had pain going into the buttock for two days, severe, and no numbness in the legs or weakness in the legs."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 270.33,
      "end_seconds": 272.51,
      "duration_seconds": 2.18,
      "text": "That's what happened, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 287.75,
      "end_seconds": 308.39,
      "duration_seconds": 20.64,
      "text": "An MRI of the lumbar spine is what I'd like next, for persistent back pain. An X-ray of the lower back is what I'd like next, for back pain. You'll be taking thiocolchicoside, 4 milligrams, twice a day, for five days. That should help with muscle spasm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 310.19,
      "end_seconds": 342.75,
      "duration_seconds": 32.56,
      "text": "I'll start you on ibuprofen, 400 milligrams, twice a day after food, for five days. You take it by mouth. It's for back pain. It's a commonly used medicine and most people tolerate it well. Staying gently active heals back pain faster than bed rest, so keep moving. I'm going to send a referral to physiotherapy. Is there anything you'd like me to go over again?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 343.42,
      "end_seconds": 345.81,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "Thank you, that's helpful."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 347.33,
      "end_seconds": 348.79,
      "duration_seconds": 1.46,
      "text": "See you soon."
    }
  ]
}